   - Length variance (difference between outputs and references).
 - Report generation: structured JSON + Markdown summaries.
 - CLI command `frai eval` wrapping the core harness.
+- Optional thresholds to gate CI jobs on metric scores.
 
 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Gating (CI Integration)
+The `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option allows CI pipelines to gate on evaluation results:
+- Specify one or more thresholds (e.g., `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.8`).
+- Exit code 0 if all thresholds pass, exit code 1 if any fail.
+- Malformed thresholds or unknown metrics: exit code 2 with descriptive error.
+- Metrics without scores (e.g., exact_match when no references) fail their thresholds.
+- Reports include threshold results: JSON adds top-level `passed` field and `thresholds` array; Markdown adds "Thresholds" section.
+- Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations` via `generateReport(..., thresholds)`.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object to enable CI gating without modifying CLI.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
